# Both the API and the socket are same-origin by default: the browser calls /api/... and
# /ws/incidents on its own origin, and Vite's dev proxy forwards them to Spring on 8080.
# That is what makes CORS a non-problem rather than a configured one, so there is normally
# nothing to set here.
#
# Set this only for a split deploy, where the dashboard is served from a different origin
# than the API. Doing so reintroduces the cross-origin case: the socket would then need
# its origin listed in incident.websocket.allowed-origins, and the REST calls would need
# real CORS config on the backend. See docs/frontend.md.
#
# Copy to .env.local to use. Only VITE_-prefixed vars reach browser code.
# VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8080/ws/incidents
